WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.000
Hey YouTubers. It's Charlie.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.360
Thank you everyone that left questions on my episode 5 video.

00:00:05.364 --> 00:00:08.500
I know everyone had a lot of questions about greyscale, Ancient Valyria,

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:12.000
and what might be happening -- like the big WTFs later this season.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.600
So I tried to add all those questions.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.300
So here we go. Careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the episode yet.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.880
First question: Joosef asks, "The stone men did touch Tyrion and he seems to be immune.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.140
Does this confirm that he might be a secret Targ?"

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.920
No, I think that the show just didn't want to give him greyscale.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.800
If they wanted him to have greyscale, they probably would have given him that Jorah Mormont moment.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.260
It doesn't mean Tyrion's completely safe but he's probably safe for now.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.820
Next question: jason asks, "Do you think that Theon/Reek will tell Sansa the truth about her brothers?

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.120
And if he does, do you think that she would believe him?"

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.060
Oh, you mean the fact that he didn't really kill her brothers.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.060
No, I think she'll find out though.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.800
There are probably people in and around Winterfell that know that her brothers are still alive.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.800
But right now I feel like the show has tried to make Sansa as uncomfortable as possible.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.460
If she were to find out her brothers were alive, that would be a big source of comfort.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.680
I don't think the show wants to give that to her yet.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.620
No matter how stone cold she seemed in this episode,

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.220
things are probably going to get worse for her before they get better.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.380
Next question: adam asks, "Can you explain the grey skin disease?"

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.200
So, you're talking about greyscale.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.920
The way I think of it is like a form of leprosy that is just really contagious.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.920
Gilly did a really good job of explaining its effects, its prolonged effects,

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.260
so you should just rewatch that scene too.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:31.860
Your skin and soft tissues slowly harden 'til it looks like you have scales, like, stony skin.  That's why they call them the stone men.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.600
Eventually your body just shuts down.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:40.100
Gilly says that her sisters went mad too but the madness could be just side effects from having a prolonged disease like that

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.080
and being left to die out in the cold.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.380
Like, if you had a debilitating disease, no matter what it might do to your body, your mind might be fine.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:50.540
But if you were left out in the cold to die, you'd probably go a little nuts too.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:55.300
As weird as the stone men that we saw in this episode seemed, I think that they were just super desperate.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:01.060
Next question: Youssef asks, "Do you think that Stannis and his army will be facing the White Walkers before they reach Winterfell?"

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.980
No, I think all the White Walkers that we see will be north of The Wall up at Hardhome.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.240
Winter's pretty much here. I mean, I feel like on the show, they're going to have a moment where they say, "Winter is here"

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.240
just because "Winter is coming" is such a big saying.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.660
It just feels like a really cliché slam dunk to give a character.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.440
"Winer has come," and then, you know, cue scary 'Inception' music like at the end of this episode.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.580
So, Stannis isn't just going to march down there unscathed.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:29.860
Next question: Cristiano asks, "Do you think that the dragon feeding scene was the most disturbing one that Sophie talked about

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.180
or is there something even more gruesome up north coming?"

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.680
Oh, so you're talking about -- yeah, Sophie Turner was talking about a really gruesome moment.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.360
No, I think her moment will be something specific to her storyline.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.360
There were a number of actors, like the Onion Knight, for intance,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.660
in real life the actor said that there is going to be some really gruesome moment happening.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.400
Because his story takes place within Stannis' camp, you know, around those characters,

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.800
I think his moment that he was talking about is specific to that.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:03:00.000
So whatever Sophie Turner was talking about is something that will be specific to Ramsay, Reek, and Sansa probably.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.480
You know, maybe Fat Walda, maybe Roose Bolton too.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.620
You have to remember that a lot of the actors don't film together.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.840
So, if an actor films on the other side of the world, they don't know what's going on in the rest of the episodes.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.420
They haven't seen the whole season.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.580
Usually, when an actor gets script pages, it's just for the scenes they're doing that day or that week.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.660
So, they don't have script pages for what's going on in an episode that they're not being filmed for.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:27.720
Next question: Zacry asks, " I was wondering why Daenerys still leaves the other two dragons (Rhaegal and Viserion) locked and chained up in the dungeon."

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:32.020
Well, that's just to appease the people.  She  locked them up because Drogon ate that peasant boy.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:36.280
If Drogon had been around at the time, she would have locked him up too.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.620
She may have felt like at that time that she was unable to control them but I think that she's slowly coming around on that.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.840
Really though, the biggest reason they're still in there is just because she wants to keep everyone happy

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.540
which, clearly, as we can see from the Sons of the Harpy, isn't working at all.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:54.360
Next question: Reuben asks, "Episode 9 was revealed to be called 'The Dance of the Dragons.'

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.360
As it is an episode 9, what do you think will happen?"

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.900
Well, I can't confirm that that's the title of the episode.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:06.800
If that's the case and it's like a typical episode 9 WTF, there will probably be metaphorical dragons dancing,

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:12.480
as in people, like Targaryens, and literal dragons dancing, as in, like, dragons flying around.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:16.020
That's just speculation. I couldn't find any confirmation about the title of the episode.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:21.860
Remember, episodes like 'Kill the Boy' have metaphorical and literal meanings.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.940
I think the metaphorical interpretation of the title is actually more interesting.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:29.160
If they're talking about dancing Targaryens, like Targaryen characters,

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:35.280
we have to consider is the show going to offer us more evidence that there is a secret Targaryen on the show?

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.940
Next question, PandaKris asks, "This season seems to be building up for a big moment with Shireen.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.040
What do you think is going to happen? What do you think it's building up to?"

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.740
Well, you know, I think Stannis' faith is going to be tested by Melisandre.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.740
Remember the reason that they took Gendry.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:55.680
Melisandre only told Selyse to take Shireen with them after they lost Gendry.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:00.320
Remember, the Onion Knight let him go and he rode off right out of the story. We have no idea where he is.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.120
He sailed right off the page.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:05.180
So, it seems like Shireen is backup for royal blood.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:10.940
For some reason, it seemed like Melisandre was unable to make a second shadow baby with Stannis.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:13.720
Clearly, that's not the direction she would go with Shireen.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:17.280
She would probably try to use her blood to do something that we haven't seen before.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:20.220
Hopefully, maybe that will be a WTF moment.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:23.300
I'm a really big fan of Shireen and the show is doing that on purpose.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.100
Like, they had that moment with Stannis because they want you to really like Stannis, think like he's a really good guy.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.480
They want you to really love Shireen because she's totally adorable.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:36.860
So what have we learned about Game of Thrones in the 4-1/2 seasons we've been watching it?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.620
The minute you love someone a lot, it's just going to yank the rug right out from under you.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.820
So, brace thyself. Winter is coming... for someone.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.120
Next question: John asks, "What is The Doom?"

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.340
You're talking about the Doom of Valyria.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:55.820
So that's a cataclysmic event when the Fourteen Flames all erupted.  Those are volcanoes in and around the Valyrian peninsula.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:00.940
Think of what happened at Pompeii. One volcano exploded and buried a civilization.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:06.720
Valyria had many, many volcanoes that all erupted around the same time.  There are a lot of theories as to why it happened.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:14.740
The most practical is that over the thousand years of the rise and height of the Valyrian Empire, they just over-mined the area around the volcanoes.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:21.980
If you remember 'Fellowship of the Ring', Gandalf talked about how the Dwarves delved too deep into the earth 'til they woke the Balrog.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.980
Something kind of like that.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:29.820
The Valyrians got too greedy, mined too deep, destabilized the earth, and it caused the volcanoes to explode.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:35.900
There are theories that people that Valyria had conquered used magic to help make the volcanoes explode

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:41.540
but because of a confluence of events, the volcanoes exploded, and that's what destroyed Valyria -- the volcanoes themselves.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:48.980
Next question: Igor asks, "Do you think that Dany is starting to behave like the Mad King? Seriously, that scene reminded me of poor old Rickard Stark."

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.820
Yeah, you know, "I choose fire as my champion! Roast him alive!"

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:57.900
No, I think they want you to think that, they want you to mentally draw that parallel, but I don't think that she's literally turning into the Mad King.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:03.380
The hope is that if Tyrion gets there, he can give her good advice and she'll slowly back off

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:08.540
but I do think that there are going to be a number of WTF moments that will still happen in and around Meereen.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.300
Daenerys standing over Hizdahr there, you know, it does kind of look like she's a little mad

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:16.300
but I think that she just feels very sure in the decision that she's made.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:19.760
Thank you so much everyone for submitting questions. These are always a ton of fun to do.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.760
I'm expecting some more changes from the books but some really great WTF moments

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.740
so I'll try to explain what the changes are whenever we see them in episodes.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:31.920
Congratulations to the book giveaway winners -- Nixa and Gabriel Benitez.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.600
You guys win your choice of 'A Feast for Crows' or 'A Dance with Dragons', both hard back, signed by George R. R. Martin.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:40.700
Whoever DMs me first can just choose which book they want and the other one will get the other book.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.840
So, DM me so we can find a way to ship the books out to you guys.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.660
Next week's giveaway will be back to the HBO Now subscriptions.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:50.940
If there are any special bonus videos you guys want to request, just let me know in the comments.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.580
Episode 6 video next week -- be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.580
The title of that episode is 'Unbent, Unbowed, Unbroken' -- the motto of House Martell

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.080
so probably going to be some really exciting Dorne stuff going on.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:05.620
Just in case you guys haven't seen it, you can click here for my episode 5 video from last night

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.300
and you can click here to learn all about Lyanna Stark.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:11.680
Thank you so much for watching, everybody. Let's high-five. I'll see you guys tomorrow.

